  "body": "The follow-up flagged in #67. Content addressing keyed on the **whole body** deduplicated 1.4% of a real log, because a retry re-sends the same context and gets a *different* answer back — so bodies rarely match even when prompts do.\n\n## Measured across the whole corpus, not a sample\n\n```\nrequests with a prompt : 50,402\ndistinct prompts       : 35,445\nrepeat rate            : 29.7% of requests\nprompt bytes           : 1.64 GB   (98% of all body bytes)\nduplicate bytes        : 0.58 GB   (35.3%)\n```\n\nI had predicted ~62.7% from a sample of recent traffic. Corpus-wide it is 35.3% of bytes — worth doing, but not what I said, so I measured before building rather than after.\n\n## Result on the real database\n\nAlready compressed by 4.47.0, then split:\n\n| | size | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Before this PR | 299 MB | |\n| After | **209 MB** | 29.9% smaller |\n\n35,461 distinct prompts across 50,460 requests. **All 50,460 bodies verified identical afterwards, zero mismatches.** Cumulative from the original uncompressed database: **1.73 GB → 209 MB (8.3x)**.\n\n## Design\n\n- Prompt in one content-addressed blob; reply, reasoning and tool calls in another.\n- **Both layouts coexist without a version flag.** A blob written before the split still carries its prompt inside it, and the *absence* of that key is what identifies a reply-only blob. Reads merge the two.\n- **Search considers both blobs together** — `proxy 8082` can have one word in the prompt and the other in the reasoning, and requiring every word within a single blob would have silently stopped finding it. Covered by a test.\n- Compaction splits existing combined blobs in a second pass.\n- `NOT NULL` relaxed on the reply reference, which a prompt-only request now legitimately leaves empty. SQLite cannot drop that in place, so the table is rebuilt — found by running against the real database, not by reading.\n\n## On turning compression up\n\nIt looked free for a one-time pass. Measured on real prompts:\n\n```\nlevel    ratio    MB/s    est. 500k rows\n    9   10.08x     9.0          19 min\n   12   10.24x     1.4         127 min\n   19   10.57x     1.0         173 min\n```\n\n**4.9% smaller for 9x the time.** Compaction keeps level 9.\n\nLocal suite **3,420 passed**, with the 6 known PowerShell installer failures that predate this branch.\n\nMINOR: 4.47.1 → 4.48.0.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
